# third_party/Detours

Microsoft Detours sources land here in Sprint 2 task **T2.2**.

Do NOT commit Detours source as part of the scaffold PR. The expected layout
once vendored is:

```
third_party/Detours/
  COMMIT.pin              # SHA of the upstream commit we depend on
  LICENSE                 # MIT — copied verbatim from microsoft/Detours
  src/
    detours.h
    detours.cpp
    detver.h
    disasm.cpp
    disolarm.cpp
    disolarm64.cpp
    disolia64.cpp
    disolx64.cpp
    disolx86.cpp
    image.cpp
    creatwth.cpp
    modules.cpp
```

Vendor command (run on the 3080 Ti box from this directory's parent):

```
git clone --depth 1 https://github.com/microsoft/Detours third_party/Detours
git -C third_party/Detours rev-parse HEAD > third_party/Detours/COMMIT.pin
```

The root `CMakeLists.txt` already detects `third_party/Detours/src/detours.cpp`
and links it as a static `detours` target when present.

License: MIT (compatible with this project's Apache-2.0).
Upstream: https://github.com/microsoft/Detours
